<%
// Sub-tab bar for Main Admin's Settings area (reached via the gear icon
// - views/partials/portal-nav.ejs's settingsHref, routes/main-admin.js's
// /settings redirect). Admins, Website, FAQ, and Quick Links are real
// separate pages/routes under the hood (unchanged), not panels of one
// shared template - this is just the tab strip every one of them
// includes at the top of <main> so switching between them still reads as
// one settings area. `activeSettingsTab` local: 'admins' | 'website' |
// 'faq' | 'quicklinks'.
//
// A real request: "make every member a user... take away user settings.
// all members will have accounts." The standalone Users tab (account
// list + role editor) is gone - every member already has an account
// managed from their own profile (routes/main-admin-members.js), and
// membership/account approval already has its own home at Members >
// Approvals (utils/membershipApprovals.js).
//
// A later real request folded admin-position permission editing into
// this same Admins page: "you can click on each admin position... the
// roles and permissions are listed below... we won't need a separate
// roles/permissions tab under settings." /main-admin/roles itself is
// unchanged and still reachable directly - it still owns the
// permissions granted to every OTHER role (teacher, parent, coop_admin),
// unrelated to admin positions - it's just no longer linked from this
// tab strip, since managing an admin position's own permissions never
// needs it anymore.
%>
<div class="view-tabs">
  <%# A real request: "co-op admin portal. settings gear, admins tab.
      this tab should be located under the main admin portal settings
      gear as a tab. it should not be on co-op admin portal." Moved from
      Co-op Admin's own Settings (routes/admin.js used to have a
      'leaders' tab there) - unchanged otherwise, still just the Admin
      Positions/Leaders manager (utils/adminPositions.js). %>
  <a class="view-tab<%= activeSettingsTab === 'admins' ? ' active' : '' %>" href="/main-admin/admins">Admins</a>
  <a class="view-tab<%= activeSettingsTab === 'website' ? ' active' : '' %>" href="/main-admin/website">Website</a>
  <%# A real request: "faq should be it's own tab under settings, not
      under website tab." Split out of the Website page (routes/main-
      admin.js used to render it as one more section on that same page) -
      unchanged CRUD/data (utils' own faqs table), just its own tab/route
      now. %>
  <a class="view-tab<%= activeSettingsTab === 'faq' ? ' active' : '' %>" href="/main-admin/faq">FAQ</a>
  <a class="view-tab<%= activeSettingsTab === 'quicklinks' ? ' active' : '' %>" href="/main-admin/quick-links">Quick Links</a>
</div>
